# Python Style and Naming

Ruff owns format and lint via `[tool.ruff]` in `pyproject.toml` - do not fight the formatter. Line
length, quote style, import grouping, function-size limits and PEP 8 naming are all configured there and
enforced by the `N`, `I`, `ANN` and `PL` rulesets. Read the config when you need a value; a copy of it
here would only go stale. The `PostToolUse` hook runs `ruff format` + `ruff check` after every edit, so
you do not need to be told to run it.

## Not enforced by a linter - which is why these are written down

- **No floating work.** Always `await` an async call, or return the coroutine to the caller. A dropped
  coroutine fails silently at runtime, not at lint time.
- **Absolute imports from `app.*` only** (`ban-relative-imports = "all"`).
- **Prefer explicit over clever.** `max-statements`/`max-complexity` catch the extremes; taste covers the
  rest.
- **Names carry contract meaning**, so they are not free choices:
  - Response/request models: `{Name}Response` / `{Name}Request` (e.g. `PingResponse`) in `app/dtos/`.
  - Exception classes: `{Name}Error` subclassing `CoreError` in `app/exceptions/`.
  - Enum members: `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` on a `PascalCase` class (e.g.
    `ErrorCodes.CLIENT_INITIALIZATION_ERROR`).
  - Settings fields must match the env var they read - see `backend/settings-config`.
- **Markdown, rule and hook script filenames are `kebab-case`.**
